  "notes": "{余|あま}る is an intransitive verb meaning to be left over or remain.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {余|あま}す (transitive, to leave over)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n- {余|あま}っている means 'there is left over' (resulting state)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- お{金|かね}が{余|あま}る: money is left over\n- {時間|じかん}が{余|あま}る: time remains\n- {力|ちから}に{余|あま}る: beyond one's ability\n- {余|あま}り{物|もの}: leftovers\n\nNOTE: The word {余|あま}り (too much, not very) is related to this verb.",
